LONG BEACH, CA – Today, Congressman Robert Garcia (CA-42) released his 2026 Pride Month playlist, celebrating Pride Month, the beginning of summer, and LGBTQ+ communities across the globe. The playlist is available on Spotify and Apple Music , and includes hits from artists like PinkPantheress, Olivia Rodrigo, Britney Spears, Bad Bunny, Selena, and more. “Music is one of the most powerful ways we can celebrate and embrace who we are and what we live for,” said Congressman Robert Garcia . “This Pride Playlist is a journey from start to finish and there’s a song in there for everyone. I hope everyone can find the same sense of pride and celebration in this playlist that I do.” A full list of tracks on the playlist can be found below: “I Just Might” – Bruno Mars “DAISIES” – Justin Bieber “bad idea right?” – Olivia Rodrigo “Stateside” – PinkPantheress “MADELINE” – INJI “Toy Soldier” – Britney Spears “BBA (feat. Megan Thee Stallion)” – Paris Hilton, Megan Thee Stallion “RUNWAY” – Lady Gaga, Doechii “The Queendom (JROB Remix)” – RuPaul “Wasabi” – Little Mix “Hypnotize - 2007 Remaster” – The Notorious B.I.G. “LATINA FOREVA” – KAROL G “DtMF” – Bad Bunny “BIZCOCHITO” – ROSALÍA “Como La Flor - Remastered Version” – Selena “Ego” – Beyoncé “You Need To Calm Down” – Taylor Swift “Animal” – Neon Trees “Your Body Is a Wonderland” – John Mayer Congressman Robert Garcia’s 2026 Pride Playlist is the third annual list that he has released. 2023’s Pride Playlist can be found here and 2024’s can be found here . Congressman Garcia has a strong belief in music as an incredible and powerful way to change people’s perceptions on issues and support communities. Congressman Garcia’s annual Pride Playlist is one way he fights to uplift the LGBTQ+ community and show people, especially young people and those who can’t live their full truth, what being proud to be queer can look like. ### Issues : Expanding Protections for the LGBTQI+ Community 33.767301314139 -118.19576409654 CA42 About Biograph