WASHINGTON, D.C. – Today, Congressman Robert Garcia (CA-42) announced that his Piers Reinvestment Act has been included as a provision in the BUILD America 250 Act, which passed a major legislative hurdle, passing out of the Transportation and Infrastructure Committee, and is one step closer to becoming law. The provision would help coastal communities repair and upgrade aging piers by expanding access to federal infrastructure funding. “Our piers support small businesses, local economies, and entire coastal communities,” said Congressman Robert Garcia . “I’m thrilled that this provision is moving forward as part of the BUILD America 250 Act and getting closer to the finish line. This is a real win for Long Beach and coastal communities up and down California and across the country.” The provision would make municipally owned piers eligible for federal grant funding through the Department of Transportation to help support local governments and coastal economies. ### Issues : Defending our Oceans, Beaches, and Wetlands 33.767301314139 -118.19576409654 CA42 About Biography Biografía en Español Talambuhay sa Tagalog ជីវប្រវត្តិ Committees and Caucuses Congressional Caucus on Peru Congressional PORTS Caucus Congressional YIMBY Caucus Popular Arts Caucus Our District Invitations and Meeting Requests Press Media Inquiries Press Releases In the News Photos Official Congressional Headshot Issues Defending our Democracy Upholding Civil Rights Defending our Oceans, Beaches, and Wetlands Supporting Small Businesses Defending the Right to Abortion Protecting Public Health Eliminating Student Debt Fighting for Immigrant Families Ending the Gun Violence Epidemic Ensuring Healthcare for All Expanding Protections for the LGBTQ+ Community Fighting to Get Big Money out of Politics Providing Safe, Affordable Housing for Every American Raising Wages for Working Families Reducing Emissions Through Green Jobs and Technology Strengthening our Safety Net for Vulnerable Americans Supporting