LONG BEACH, CA – Today, Congressman Robert Garcia (CA-42) announced $2.175 million in federal funding for California State University, Long Beach (CSULB) to support the construction of a new Long Beach Research Center and Special Collections Archives. This funding will help create a modern facility that will preserve rare materials and expand access to the histories that shape CSULB and the Long Beach region. “This funding is about investing in education, access, and opportunity for our entire community,” said Congressman Robert Garcia . “CSULB plays a critical role in Long Beach, and this new research center will give students and the public a place to learn, explore, and engage with history in meaningful ways. I’m proud to support a project that strengthens our university and will open doors for future generations.” Last year, the House Committee on Appropriations announced they would begin accepting Community Project Funding requests from Members of Congress to meet the needs of communities across the country. Congressman Garcia and his staff have reached out and met with numerous stakeholders from each corner of the district to discuss projects throughout each of the communities the Congressman represents. ### Issues : Eliminating Student Debt 33.767301314139 -118.19576409654 CA42 About Biography Biografía en Español Talambuhay sa Tagalog ជីវប្រវត្តិ Committees and Caucuses Congressional Caucus on Peru Congressional PORTS Caucus Congressional YIMBY Caucus Popular Arts Caucus Our District Invitations and Meeting Requests Press Media Inquiries Press Releases In the News Photos Official Congressional Headshot Issues Defending our Democracy Upholding Civil Rights Defending our Oceans, Beaches, and Wetlands Supporting Small Businesses Defending the Right to Abortion Protecting Public Health Eliminating Student Debt Fighting for Immigrant Families Ending the Gun Violence Epidemic Ensuring Healthcare for All Expanding Protections for the LGBTQ+ Community Fighting to Ge