Washington D.C.- Congressman Robert Garcia (CA-42) today released the following statement following the announcement that he will be serving on the House Committee on Homeland Security. Congressman Robert Garcia has also been appointed to the House Committee on Oversight and Accountability. “I am honored to have been appointed to the House Committee on Homeland Security. There is no greater priority than the security of the United States and ensuring the American people are protected from enemies foreign and domestic,” said Congressman Garcia. “We are at a pivotal time in our nation’s history: Democracy is under attack, white supremacists pose the biggest domestic terror threat, and we just commemorated two year’s since the shameful attack on our nation’s Capitol. I am committed to fighting and pushing back on the lies that will be made by GOP Homeland Security members like Marjorie Taylor Greene to ensure that the American people are truly protected. As a proud immigrant and patriot, I will fight to defend our nation’s legacy and values that extreme MAGA republicans continue to put under attack.” The GOP has made clear that they will be using taxpayer money to focus on nonsense partisan investigations ranging from calling for DHS Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas to be impeached over the GOP’s' disagreement with President Biden's policies on border security and immigration, to stoking divisive culture war topics that will do nothing for the American people. To this day, Republican Chair Mark Green continues to deny the results of the 2020 election, and his colleague Marjorie Taylor Green also has yet to relent her false claim that the 2020 election was stolen from Donald Trump. Congressman Garcia is committed to serving as a strong voice to fight back against these attacks on truth and facts. Congressman Garcia immigrated to the United States as a young child and was raised in Southern California, becoming a proud U.S. citizen in his 20's. He holds an M.A. from the University of Southern California and an Ed.D. in Higher Education from Cal State Long Beach, where he also earned his B.A. in Communications. Congressman Garcia believes in defending our democracy and fighting to expand and protect essential rights for women, immigrants, and the LGBTQI+ community. ### Issues : Defending Democracy Ending the Gun Violence Epidemic 33.767301314139 -118.19576409654 CA42 About Biography Biografía en Español Talambuhay sa Tagalog ជីវប្រវត្តិ Committees and Caucuses Congressional Caucus on Peru Congressional PORTS Caucus Congressional YIMBY Caucus Popular Arts Caucus Our District Invitations and Meeting Requests Press Media Inquiries Press Releases In the News Photos Official Congressional Headshot Issues Defending our Democracy Upholding Civil Rights Defending our Oceans, Beaches, and Wetlands Supporting Small Businesses Defending the Right to Abortion Protecting Public Health Eliminating Student Debt Fighting for Immigrant Families Ending the Gun Violence Epidemic Ensuring Healthcare for All Expanding Protections for the LGBTQ+ Community Fighting to Get Big Money out of Politics Providing Safe, Affordable Housing for Every American Raising Wages for Working Families Reducing Emissions Through Green Jobs and Technology Strengthening our Safety Net for Vulnerable Americans Supporting Unions and Working People Services Appropriations Requests Community Project Funding Request Form Help with a Federal Agency Grant Applicants Veterans Military Academy Nominations Tours and Tickets Flags Art Competition Get Affordable Internet Federal Government Shutdown: Frequently Asked Questions Transparency FY24 Community Projects FY25 Community Projects FY26 Community Projects FY27 Nominated Community Project Funding Votes and Legislation Washington DC Office 109 Cannon House Office Building Washington, DC 20515 Phone: (202) 225-7924 Long Beach District Office 415 West Ocean Blvd. Suite 2803 Long Beach, CA 90802 Phone: (562) 512-8489 Copyright Privacy House.